question:
Consider a sequence \( a_n \) defined for positive integers \( n \) as follows:

\[
a_n = \begin{cases} 
3 & \text{if } n = 1, \\
a_{n - 1} + 2 & \text{if } n \text{ is odd and } n > 1, \\
a_{n - 1} - 1 & \text{if } n \text{ is even} 
\end{cases}
\]

Determine the minimum value of \( a_n \) for all \( n = 1, 2, 3, \ldots, 2023 \).

Consider the function \( h(x) \) defined piecewise as follows:
\[
h(x) = \begin{cases} 
2x - 1 & \text{if } x \text{ is even} \\
\frac{x + 1}{2} & \text{if } x \text{ is odd} 
\end{cases}
\]
Let \( k(x) = h(h(x)) \). If \( m \) is a positive integer such that \( k^2(m) = 1 \) and the operation \( k^2 \) denotes applying the function \( k \) twice, determine the smallest possible value of \( m \).

In the diagram below, circle \( \Gamma \) has center \( O \) and radius \( 10 \). Points \( A \) and \( B \) lie on \( \Gamma \), and chord \( AB \) is \( 12 \) units long. Line \( CO \) is perpendicular to \( AB \) at point \( D \) on \( AB \). Find the length of \( CD \).

[asy]
unitsize(1inch);
pair O, A, B, C, D;
O = (0,0);
A = (-3, sqrt(91));
B = (3, sqrt(91));
D = (0, sqrt(91));
C = (0, sqrt(91)+sqrt(9));
draw(Circle(O,10));
draw(A--B);
draw(O--C, dotted);
draw(O--D);
draw(C--D);
label("$A$",A,NW);
label("$B$",B,NE);
label("$O$",O,S);
label("$C$",C,N);
label("$D$",D,S);
[/asy]

